  "description": "ZEZTUX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C106 H112 Dy8 N12 O40,2(C2 H6 O1),2(C1 H2 Cl2). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.527-3.891 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.91-113.61°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C112H128Cl4Dy8N12O42. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
